  "cil_liability": null,
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed creation of a dropped kerb and vehicle crossover, by reason of facilitating vehicles manoeuvring in and/or out of the site, over the public footway, would have a detrimental impact on highway and pedestrian safety and the safe and efficient operation of the public highway. As such the proposal is contrary to Policies T1 (Strategic approach to transport), T2 (Healthy Streets), and T4 (Assessing and mitigating transport impacts) of the London Plan (2021) and policies LP41 (Liveable Neighbourhoods), LP43 (Transport and Development) and LP44 (Public Transport and Infrastructure) of the Hackney Local Plan 2033 (2020).&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10.5pt; white-space: pre-wrap;&quot;&gt;The proposed creation of a dropped kerb and vehicle crossover, by reason of the loss of on-street parking spaces, fails to promote sustainable modes of transport and does not promote car free residential development, contrary to policies T6 (Car parking), T6.1 (Residential Parking) of the London Plan (2021) and policies LP43 (Transport and Development) and LP45 (Parking and Car Free Development) of the Hackney Local Plan 2033 (2020) alongside the National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
